Most importantly, check your terminal. With the modified backend you will know immediately whether the problem is:

1. Existing valid token

or:

2. send_verification_email() returns False

or:

3. send_verification_email() returns True but the SMTP/provider does not actually deliver

Your current Uvicorn output strongly suggests that the first thing to inspect is email_service.py, because a 200 OK alone does not establish that an email was delivered.